+# Image generation prompts
+
+Generated with the built-in image generation tool. All four images were generated independently from text, without reference images, and saved as 1024×1024 PNGs using sips.
+
+## styles/629-mo-willems.png
+
+Create a fresh square 1024x1024 illustration from text only. Style: Mo Willems picture book. Extremely simple hand-drawn cartoon, enormous amounts of empty pure white space, a single thick uneven black contour quality, utterly flat colors, a deadpan expression, radical economy of marks and childlike anatomy. The character is a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. She is huge on the page, a large simplified seated figure in an understated side-on pose, holding her coffee cup; a croissant rests within reach. Knit indicated with only a few simple marks. Let the picture-book style dictate proportions and framing. No photographic realism, rendering, gradients, shading, or detailed scenery. No text, words, lettering, captions, speech balloons, signatures, or watermarks. Generate ONE image only. No reference images.
+
+## styles/630-dav-pilkey.png
+
+Generate ONE fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024. Dav Pilkey children's book drawing: energetic uneven felt-tip marker, goofy action lines, bright childish color, messy on purpose. A playful handmade drawing with wonky proportions, gigantic silly head, cartoon noodle limbs, crude black marker strokes, scribbled color escaping outlines, joyful physical comedy. A woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater is enjoying coffee, with a croissant nearby. She is large and prominent: FULL BODY, flying into a gleeful awkward hop with bent knees and one foot kicked up, gripping a little steaming coffee cup in one hand and balancing a croissant on a small saucer in the other. Diagonal movement across the square, sparse wonky cafe details and childishly drawn bright color patches. Big goofy pleased facial expression. Style controls all anatomy, composition, palette and medium. A convincingly rough exuberant children's-book marker drawing. No photography, no realistic anatomy, no polished digital gradients. No text, no speech balloons, no words, no sound effect lettering, no captions, no signatures or watermarks. Do not use any reference images or earlier images.
+
+## styles/631-philippe-druillet.png
+
+Create ONE original square 1024x1024 image from text alone. Philippe Druillet comic painting: monumental baroque science-fiction architecture, massive areas of heavy black ink, obsessively dense ornament, explosive acid color, cosmic scale, elaborate geometric arabesques and impossible perspectives, hand-painted vintage European science-fiction comic page without lettering. Main subject: a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. She is LARGE in the foreground as an imposing waist-up figure viewed from a dramatic low angle, her stylized elongated face and ornate tangled curls framed by the architecture, raising a coffee goblet to her lips with a quietly content expression. Croissant on a sculptural cafe ledge right beside her. Behind her: towering concentric cathedral-like alien megastructures, intricately inked machinery, alien buttresses, radiating spires, elaborate cosmic vaults and a lurid celestial sky. She dominates the lower foreground; the ornate architecture towers over and around her, integrating figure and environment as one bold graphic composition. Acid magenta, electric cyan, toxic lime and sulfur yellow against broad jet-black ink. Dense crosshatching and boldly flattened color with hand-painted texture. STYLE IS THE PRIORITY: let it control anatomy, face, framing, color and space. This must be an authentic illustrated comic painting, never a photograph with an effect. No text, lettering, captions, speech balloons, signatures, or watermarks. Use no reference images and no earlier image as a reference.
+
+## styles/632-enki-bilal.png
+
+Generate ONE fresh square 1024x1024 image from text only. Enki Bilal painted comic: cold blue-gray palette, weathered faces, muddy future city, scratched painted textures, ashen chalky skin, bruised blue shadows, dry-brush gouache and scumbled acrylic with fine uneasy pencil contours. A woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater is quietly enjoying a coffee, with a croissant nearby. INTIMATE CLOSE-UP IN LEFT-FACING PROFILE: her large head and near shoulder fill the right two-thirds of the frame, unruly auburn curls, angular weathered facial structure still clearly early 30s, freckles, cloudy round tortoiseshell lenses; she holds a chipped coffee cup just below her lips, takes a moment of private satisfaction with lowered eyes. The cup and her fingers are clearly visible in the lower foreground; a croissant rests on a narrow battered ledge beside them. Beyond the face in the left background, muddy futuristic city tenements and crumbling industrial towers dissolve into blue-gray polluted fog, rain and grime. The mustard knit and auburn hair are muted earthy accents within the pervasive icy blue-gray palette. An authentic hand-painted European dystopian comic panel with stylized anatomy, painterly irregularities, erasures, abraded surfaces and scratched texture integrated throughout the art. Style dictates anatomy, framing and lighting completely. No photographic rendering, no smooth 3D or glossy digital finish. No text, captions, letters, numbers, signage, speech balloons, signatures, or watermarks. Do not use any reference image or any previous image.
+

